00:25:01,424 --> 00:25:01,504
Yeah.

253
00:25:01,744 --> 00:25:12,864
So it actually maybe somewhat fortuitous that the approach that protein MPNN, which is this structure to sequence model uses, is actually pretty analogous to the way that transformer-based models generate text.

254
00:25:13,024 --> 00:25:14,864
So protein MPNN is a third-party tool.

255
00:25:15,022 --> 00:25:16,384
It's not something that Google developed.

256
00:25:16,464 --> 00:25:20,944
Uh, it's been released out in the world for a number of years, and it's almost the opposite of AlphaFold.

257
00:25:21,104 --> 00:25:24,864
So rather than going from a sequence to a structure, it goes from a structure to a sequence.

258
00:25:24,944 --> 00:25:33,636
And that's an important part in a protein design pipeline where you are originally choosing your target based off of how you want them to interact in three-dimensional space.

259
00:25:33,998 --> 00:25:41,584
This is a model that just takes that representation and then creates a predicted sequence in order to fold into that specific configuration.

